course: dictionary
lesson: 1961
title: Finding your way with a compass
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A compass has a needle that swings round to point north. The needle is a small magnet that is free to turn. «A compass needle is a small magnet free to turn, and it lines up with the Earth's magnetic field.» That is why it always points the same way. Use it with a map to find your direction.
explain: Compass also has another meaning. It is a drawing tool with two arms, one with a point and one with a pencil, used to draw circles. In British English you may hear «a pair of compasses». Same word, different job, so the words around it tell you which one is meant.
explain: The four main compass points are north, east, south and west. Some people remember them with «Never Eat Soggy Weetabix». Compass points help you describe where things are, such as north of the school.
explain: Use context to find the meaning. «A magnetised needle on a leaf floating in water turns to point north» is about finding direction, because it says the needle points north. When a sentence talks about drawing circles, the word means the drawing tool. Always ask: which meaning fits here?
fact: A compass needle is a small magnet, and it lines up with the Earth's magnetic field.
fact: The Earth is like a giant magnet, which is why a compass works.
fact: «Compass points» are north, east, south and west.
fact: A pair of compasses is a drawing tool with two arms, used to draw circles.
fact: Sailors used compasses like this nearly a thousand years ago.
exercise: «A compass needle is a small magnet free to turn, and it lines up with the Earth's magnetic field.» What does the needle line up with? | The sea waves | *The Earth's magnetic field | A pencil | The moon's shadow
exercise: Tom needs to draw a perfect circle in maths. Which tool should he use? | A ruler | *A pair of compasses | A map | A protractor
exercise: Which of these is one of the four main compass points? | Left | Upward | Sideways | *North
test: «The magnetic compass was used by Chinese sailors by about 1100.» What were sailors using the compass for? | *To find their direction | To tell the time | To grow crops | To cook meals
test: In maths, what does a pair of compasses help you do? | Measure the weight of a book | *Draw circles | Read a story | Count money
exam: Which sentence uses compass to mean a tool for finding direction, not a drawing tool? | *«A compass needle lines up with the Earth's magnetic field» | «Use the pencil arm to mark the paper» | «Set the arms apart to the radius» | «Draw a circle with a pair of compasses»
